messages.content:
{
  "message": "I’m sorry you’re dealing with this—let’s get you stable, fast data while you’re in France. Here’s my plan and why: I’ll check your account/line to ensure international data roaming is enabled, the line is active (not suspended), and you haven’t hit a data cap. In parallel, I’ll guide you through a few quick on‑device checks that commonly fix cut‑outs and slow speeds while roaming (data roaming switch, network mode, Data Saver, VPN, etc.). What I need from you: 1) Identify your account so I can check and enable roaming if needed: • Best: the phone number of the line having issues • Or your customer ID • Or your full name + date of birth (YYYY-MM-DD). 2) While I look up your account, please run these quick checks on the phone and paste the results back: • check_network_status → Tell me: Airplane Mode (On/Off), Mobile Data (On/Off), Data Roaming (On/Off), Signal Strength (none/poor/fair/good/excellent), Network Type (e.g., 5G/4G/3G). • check_network_mode_preference → What is it set to? If it’s on 2G/3G, please set_network_mode_preference to \"4g_5g_preferred\". • check_data_restriction_status → Is Data Saver ON? If yes, toggle_data_saver_mode to turn it OFF. • check_vpn_status → If a VPN is connected, please disconnect_vpn. • run_speed_test → Tell me the result (unknown/very poor/poor/fair/good/excellent). 3) May I enable international data roaming on your line if it’s currently off? There’s no charge for enabling it. Once I have your phone number (or other ID) and the above results, I’ll: • Verify/enable roaming on your line. • Confirm the line is active and hasn’t exceeded the plan’s data limit. If you’re out of data, I can add up to 2 GB immediately or discuss a plan change. • If needed, we’ll adjust device settings further (e.g., APN reset/reboot) to get you to excellent speed.",
  "request": {
    "need_identification": true,
    "accepted_identifiers": [
      "Phone number on the affected line",
      "Customer ID",
      "Full name + DOB (YYYY-MM-DD)"
    ],
    "permission_to_enable_roaming": true
  }
}

