      "step": 1,
      "title": "Check the status bar",
      "why": "This quickly tells us if you have signal and what network you’re on.",
      "how": "Look at the very top of your screen. Do you see signal bars? Do you see 5G, 4G/LTE, or 3G? Is there a small ‘R’ (for roaming)? Please note what you see."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "title": "Make sure Airplane Mode is OFF",
      "why": "Airplane mode disables mobile data.",
      "how": "Open Settings. Look for ‘Airplane mode’ and make sure it’s OFF. If it was on, turn it off and wait 10 seconds."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "title": "Turn Mobile Data ON",
      "why": "Mobile data must be on to use the internet away from Wi‑Fi.",
      "how": "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network (or Cellular). Make sure ‘Mobile data’ is ON."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "title": "Enable Data Roaming ON (since you’re in France)",
      "why": "Roaming must be on for data to work abroad.",
      "how": "In the same Mobile network screen, turn ‘Data roaming’ ON. If you get a warning about charges, it’s expected; we just need it ON while abroad."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "title": "Turn OFF any VPN",
      "why": "VPNs can slow or block data while roaming.",
      "how": "Settings > VPN. If a VPN shows ‘Connected’, disconnect it for now."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "title": "Turn OFF Data Saver / Low Data Mode",
      "why": "Data Saver can throttle or pause background data and make apps feel very slow.",
      "how": "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Data Saver (or Data usage). Turn Data Saver OFF."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "title": "Prefer faster networks (4G/5G)",
      "why": "Being stuck on 2G/3G is too slow for ‘excellent’ speeds.",
      "how": "Settings > Mobile network > Preferred network type. Choose 5G/4G (may be called ‘5G/4G/3G/2G auto’ or ‘5G/4G preferred’)."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "title": "Quick restart",
      "why": "A reboot refreshes the network session after changes.",
      "how": "Restart your phone. After it powers back on, wait 30–60 seconds for the network to settle."
    },
    {
      "step": 9,
      "title": "Speed check",
      "why": "We need to confirm you’re at ‘Excellent’ speed.",
      "how": "Open your browser and try fast.com or speedtest.net. Tell me the result. If the test gives a quality label, share it; otherwise share the download Mbps number."
    }
  ],
  "what_to_send_me_now": [
    "Your mobile phone number (or full name + DOB) so I can check your line’s roaming status and data balance on our side.",
    "From Step 1: What the status bar shows (signal bars, 5G/4G/3G, and whether there’s an ‘R’).",
    "Confirm that Mobile data and Data roaming are ON.",
    "Whether a VPN was on and is now off.",
    "The speed test result after Step 9."
