{
  "message": "I can help you get MMS working while you’re in France. My plan is twofold: (1) verify your line’s account settings on our side (especially roaming and data status), and (2) walk you through a few quick checks on your phone that commonly fix MMS abroad. To begin, please provide one of the following so I can look up your account and check/enable roaming on your line at no cost: • The phone number on the line having issues (preferred), or • Your customer ID, or • Your full name + date of birth (YYYY-MM-DD). Also, do I have your permission to enable international data roaming on your line if it’s currently off? While I look that up, please do these quick checks on your phone and share the results: 1) Check basic network status: • Turn Wi‑Fi OFF temporarily. • On your phone, run check_network_status and tell me: signal strength, current network type (e.g., 4G/5G/3G/2G), whether Mobile Data is enabled, and whether Data Roaming is enabled. If Mobile Data or Data Roaming is OFF, please turn them ON using toggle_data and toggle_roaming. 2) Confirm mobile data works: • With Wi‑Fi still OFF, run run_speed_test and share the result (e.g., no connection/poor/fair/good/excellent). If you can also try loading a webpage, let me know if it works. 3) Verify MMS server (MMSC) setting: • Run check_apn_settings and tell me the APN name and the MMSC URL shown. If MMSC is blank or looks wrong, please use reset_apn_settings and then reboot_device to apply changes. 4) Eliminate common blockers: • If check_wifi_calling_status shows Wi‑Fi Calling is ON, please toggle_wifi_calling OFF and try sending an MMS again. • If check_vpn_status shows a VPN is connected, please disconnect_vpn and retry. 5) Try an MMS test: • After the above, try sending yourself a picture message and let me know what happens (any error message or if it sends). Why these steps: MMS needs (a) active cellular service, (b) mobile data with roaming when abroad, and (c) a correct MMSC in your APN. Wi‑Fi Calling and VPNs can also interfere with MMS in some cases. Once you share your phone number (or other ID), I’ll immediately check your line’s roaming status, data usage against your plan, and any suspensions, and enable roaming on our side if needed."
}

