messages.content:
{
  "message": "Yes—please reset the APN and then reboot. Here’s the plan and why: Your MMSC is blank, which prevents MMS from sending/receiving even though your data/roaming are fine. Resetting APN restores the correct MMS server, and a reboot applies the change to the network stack. Do these steps in order: 1) Fix the APN: • Run reset_apn_settings. 2) Apply the change: • Run reboot_device. 3) Verify after reboot: • Ensure Wi‑Fi is still OFF. • Run check_network_status and confirm: Signal (at least fair), Network type (3G/4G/5G), Mobile Data ON, Data Roaming ON. If Mobile Data or Roaming flipped OFF, turn them back ON using toggle_data and toggle_roaming. • Run check_apn_settings again and share the APN name and MMSC URL to confirm the MMSC is now populated. 4) Test MMS: • Option A: Run can_send_mms and share the result. • Option B: Try sending yourself a picture message and tell me what happens (including any error). If MMS still fails after the reset/reboot: • Check Wi‑Fi Calling: run check_wifi_calling_status; if ON, toggle_wifi_calling OFF and retry MMS. • Check VPN: run check_vpn_status; if a VPN is connected, disconnect_vpn and retry MMS. Please proceed with reset_apn_settings now, then reboot_device, and send me the post‑reboot check_network_status and check_apn_settings results. I’ll interpret them and guide the next step."
}

