  "thought_process": "Your phone reports No SIM/Missing, which blocks any network registration—so calls, SMS, and MMS cannot work. The quickest fix is to reseat the SIM (or refresh the eSIM line), then restart to let the radio reinitialize. Once the SIM shows Active, we should see signal return and then MMS will work (you already have 2 GB refueled).",
  "step_7_reseat_sim": {
    "title": "Reseat the SIM (physical SIM) or refresh the eSIM line",
    "safety_note": "If you have a physical SIM tray, power the phone off before removing the tray.",
    "physical_sim": [
      "Power the phone OFF.",
      "Eject the SIM tray, remove the SIM, gently wipe it (dry, lint-free), and reinsert it in the correct orientation.",
      "Reinsert the tray fully and power the phone ON.",
      "Wait 60–90 seconds for the phone to search for a network."
    ],
    "esim": [
      "If you use eSIM (no physical tray):",
      "iPhone: Settings > Cellular (Mobile Data) > tap your line > toggle this line OFF, wait 10 seconds, then toggle ON.",
      "Android: Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > SIMs (or Mobile network) > toggle your line OFF, wait 10 seconds, then ON.",
      "After toggling, restart the phone (power off, wait 15 seconds, power on)."
    ],
    "after_reseat_restart": [
      "Open Settings and check SIM status again (Active vs. No SIM).",
      "Watch the status bar for signal bars and a network type (3G/4G/LTE/5G).",
      "If no signal yet, we’ll do a quick Airplane Mode cycle once more."
    ]
  },
  "what_to_reply": "Please proceed to reseat the SIM (or refresh the eSIM line) and restart as above. Then tell me: 1) does SIM status now show Active, and 2) what does the status bar show (signal bars or No Signal, any network type)? If you’re unsure whether you have a physical SIM tray, just look for a small pinhole tray on the phone’s edge—if none, you’re likely on eSIM.",
  "next_step_preview": {
    "if_active": "We’ll run one quick Airplane Mode ON/OFF cycle, confirm Data Roaming and Mobile Data are ON (they are), and then test a voice call, a simple webpage, and sending an MMS.",
    "if_still_missing": "We’ll try one more reseat/line toggle. If it still shows No SIM, I’ll transfer you to a human agent to arrange SIM/eSIM provisioning or replacement."
  }
}

